<newsitem itemid="199414" id="root" date="1996-11-19" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Servgro raises yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Servgro raises yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     51.3	  vs  36.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 15.0	  vs  11.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   62.9	  vs  42.6</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  103.5	  vs  82.9</p>
<p>    Tax			 31.7	  vs  25.6</p>
<p>    Turnover		 748.3	  vs 636.7</p>
<p>Div payable January 10</p>
<p>on register December 13</p>
<p>Full name:  Servgro International Ltd  industrial-beverages, hotels &amp; leisure)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said trading conditions would remain competitive and demanding. However, it said operating companies were well positioned to cope with this and the group was therefore expected to show substantial real growth in earnings per share for the year to March 31 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
